The software CRC-32 in this crate is not a moved core: it is the oracle the accelerator is checked against.

`crates/efr32mg2x-hal/examples/hal_gpcrc.rs` compares the GPCRC engine against this implementation, and both
conventions (MSB-first and reflected) are kept and pinned to their published vectors so that a disagreement can be
localised rather than merely noticed. Moving it into the HAL would ship a bit-by-bit CRC in every firmware image
that does not use it, which is the opposite of the reason the HAL exists.

The crate still compiles the HAL's `cores/gpcrc.rs` by `#[path]`, so the parts it shares are shared; what it adds is
the arithmetic that checks the hardware.
